## Context

Two CSV-vs-prose date divergences found so far:
- Mistral stage-1: fixed in PR #422
- Alibaba stage-3: open in ticket 0232

The root cause is that `data/capability_timeline.csv` is the declared source
of truth, but `docs/capability-timeline.md` is edited by hand. When one is
updated, the other can silently fall out of sync.

## Actions

Add `tests/test_capability_timeline_sync.py` with an `@pytest.mark.adherence`
test that:
1. Reads all non-absent dates from `data/capability_timeline.csv`
2. Checks each date appears in the matrix section of
   `docs/capability-timeline.md`
3. Skips rows where the date is `absent` or empty
4. Special-cases intentionally approximate entries (e.g. OpenAI stage-8
   `2025-03-01` shown as `2025-03` in prose): add an allowlist of
   `(lab, stage)` pairs that are exempt from exact-date matching

This test runs with `make check-fast` and catches divergences before push.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `tests/test_capability_timeline_sync.py` exists and passes
- [ ] The test catches the Alibaba stage-3 case (will fail until 0232 is resolved)
- [ ] `pytest -m adherence` passes after 0232 is resolved
- [ ] `make check` passes
